{"kind":"assert","text":"C2 rulings on d0892142, for the three points of \"Not settled\" and\nthe two test points.\n\n1. A `TransportError` from `ScopeHandle.log`: `behind` is right, and\n   the replica does not stop. A lost reply passes with time. A reply\n   that is no answer is a fault of the service, and the member's next\n   call throws the same error to the caller, where the page sees it.\n   One change: a replica that knows a head that it does not hold\n   starts a read on each `streaming` state of the observation, when\n   no read runs. Today `streaming` starts no read, so a reconnection\n   after a failed read leaves the replica `behind` until the next\n   entry. Add one test: a read fails, the observation reconnects, and\n   the replica reaches `current` with no new entry.\n   The limit that stays: a feed that stays up over a scope with no\n   new entry gives no event, so the replica stays `behind` until a\n   caller calls `read`. The replica holds no timer. Move this limit\n   from \"Not settled\" to a section \"Limits\" in the C2 note. C3\n   carries the rest: the client calls `read` on each call of the\n   member.\n\n2. `mismatch` reads `not-judged` in C2. Accepted. The replica's entry\n   for the key closes the custody record in C3, by ruling 04bb24ba.\n   C3 carries one test: a request whose key holds another intent is\n   in no published view with `predicted` `not-judged`. The record\n   closes in the same change of the view.\n\n3. `name` on `refused-here` and `never`: accepted. It is the `name`\n   of the `refused` answer in `contract/src/result.ts`. The C2 head\n   changes the `Judged` type in section 9 of the client note to the\n   built type, with `name?: string` on both cases and one sentence\n   that says what it holds.\n\n4. The generated suite stays at 400 seeds of 80 steps, as section 11\n   of the client note states. The review request states its duration\n   on AC.\n\n5. `format:check` runs in the gate. Nothing more is needed before\n   the gate.\n\nThe plan to drop the two merges and put the two C2 commits on main\nafter PG-1 and IE-1 with FG-1 land: accepted. C3 can start on this\nhead.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}